{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender glew mx support blender glew mx support","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","fileName":"Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GLEW-MX Support","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender GHOST Windowing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST Rendering Context","Blender GHOST C API","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender glew mx support blender glew mx support","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","fileName":"Blender GLEW-MX Support.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GLEW-MX Support","heading":"Blender GLEW-MX Support","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"GLEW supplies access to OpenGL extension functions that are not uniformly available through a base platform interface. Blender's internally maintained `glew-mx` layer extends that role to applications using multiple rendering contexts.\n\nGHOST depends on this support because each [[Blender GHOST Rendering Context]] may need its own extension state. Keeping the integration below the [[Blender GHOST C API]] prevents core Blender code from managing platform-specific function discovery directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST Rendering Context","Blender GHOST C API","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GLEW-MX Support.md::